    "25 I am about to open and review the project's main documentation file.",
    "26",
    "27",
    "28",
    "29",
    "30 **ACP Devtools**\n\nThis is **`acp-devtools`** — a developer tool for inspecting, debugging, and validating traffic between code editors and AI coding agents using the **Agent Client Protocol (ACP)**.\n\n**What is ACP?**\nThe [Agent Client Protocol](https://agentclientprotocol.com) is an open, newline-delimited JSON-RPC wire format that lets editors (WebStorm, Zed, IntelliJ, Neovim, VS Code via ReSharper) communicate with coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Goose, OpenCode, and 40+ others) over stdio.\n\n**What does this project do?**\n`acp-devtools` acts as a **transparent proxy** sitting in the stdio pipe between the editor and the agent — neither side knows it's there. It:\n\n- **Captures** every JSON-RPC frame in both directions\n- **Stores** sessions in SQLite\n- **Streams** data to a live web inspector UI\n- **Validates** frames against the official ACP JSON schema\n- **Provides** a CLI and a read-only MCP server\n\n**Key Features**\n- **Timeline + JSON detail** — scrollable frame list with full payload inspection, spec-aware tree view\n- **Stream clusters** — `agent_message_chunk` runs collapse into one row with a shimmer bar\n- **Spec validation** — invalid frames get badges; CLI exits with code 1 for CI gating\n- **Performance dashboard** — per-method p50/p99/max latencies, waterfall chart, auto-detected insights\n- **Multi-session diff** — frame-level + metadata + per-method p99 deltas\n- **Playground** — browser-based inspector at [playground.acp-devtools.dev](https://playground.acp-devtools.dev)\n\n**Who it's for**\n- **Agent authors** — validate wire output against the spec\n- **Editor/plugin developers** — inspect what the other side sends\n- **Debuggers** — find why a prompt took 60s, replay broken sessions\n- **CI pipelines** — gate releases on spec conformance and latency regressions\n\n**Tech Stack**\n- **Node.js ≥ 22** (TypeScript)\n- **SQLite** for session storage\n- **Vitest** for testing\n- **ESLint** for linting\n- MIT licensed, published on npm as [`acp-devtools`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/acp-devtools)",
    "31"
  ],
